# Auto commit and push

After finishing a meaningful set of code changes in this project, commit and push to `origin` on the current branch without waiting for the user to ask.

Follow the existing git safety protocol:
- Never update git config
- Never force-push to main/master unless explicitly requested
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials) or local runtime data (`.data/`)
- Use a concise commit message focused on why
- Run status/diff/log before committing; push after a successful commit
- Skip empty commits when there is nothing to push

# No Cursor attribution

Commits must stay under the repository author (`Gideon-Dadey`). Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or `Made-with: Cursor` trailers.

- Prefer creating commits in a way that does not re-inject Cursor trailers (the Husky `commit-msg` hook strips them; if tooling re-adds them on `git commit`, use `git commit-tree` / amend via tree rewrite instead)
- Before push, verify `git log -1` has no Cursor / `cursoragent@cursor.com` trailer
- Turn off Cursor Settings → Git & PRs → Attribution when working in this repo
